@startuml 07_seq_connect_join_ready_start
title Sequence: Connect, Authenticate, Join, Ready, Match Start (UC-1, UC-2, UC-9)
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 260

actor "Client A" as A
actor "Client B" as B
participant "server.Client (A)" as CA
participant "server.Client (B)" as CB
participant "SessionStore" as SS
participant "Session\n(actor)" as S
participant "Match" as M
participant "chess.Game" as G

== Connect and authenticate (shown for A; B repeats the same steps on its own connection) ==
A -> CA : TCP connect
note right of CA : Serve checks the per-IP limit and the connection semaphore,\nthen starts NewClient(...).Run
A -> CA : ConnectRequest(seq 1, protocol_version "1.0")
CA -> CA : CompatibleVersion(major version equal)
alt major version differs
  CA --> A : ErrorResponse(INVALID_PROTOCOL_VERSION), connection closed after CloseTimeout
else compatible
  CA --> A : ConnectResponse(in_reply_to 1, connection_id)
end
A -> CA : AuthRequest(seq 2, display_name)
CA -> CA : issue player_id and reconnect_token (random 128-bit IDs)
CA --> A : AuthResponse(in_reply_to 2, player_id, reconnect_token)
note over CA #FFF3CD
  PLANNED: persist (player_id, token) so a later AuthRequest can resume.
  Today a non-empty player_id or token is rejected with AUTH_FAILED.
end note

== Create a session (A) ==
A -> CA : JoinSessionRequest(seq 3, game_id "chess", session_id "")
note over CA #FFF3CD
  OPEN PR "Join an open session when no session_id is given":
  the game's policy first looks for a joinable public session.
  Only if none exists is a new session created.
end note
CA -> CA : Registry.New("chess")
CA -> SS : Create(newSessionID, "chess", game, public)
SS -> S : start Run goroutine
CA -> S : Join(clientID, displayName, seq 3, sender)
S -> S : handleJoin: assignRole against RoleSpec limits,\nappend to join order, add Member
S --> CA : nil (or ErrLobbyFull / ErrAlreadyStarted as SESSION_NOT_JOINABLE)
S --> A : StateUpdate(in_reply_to 3, WAITING, players [A])

== Join the session (B) ==
B -> CB : JoinSessionRequest(seq 3, game_id "chess", session_id "")
CB -> S : Join(clientID, displayName, seq 3, sender)
S --> B : StateUpdate(in_reply_to 3, WAITING, players [A, B])
S --> A : StateUpdate(in_reply_to 0, WAITING, players [A, B])

== Readiness and match start ==
A -> CA : SetReadyRequest(session_id, ready true)
CA -> S : SetReady(clientID, true)
S --> A : StateUpdate(WAITING, unsolicited)
S --> B : StateUpdate(WAITING, unsolicited)
note over S #FFF3CD : PR message. The reply rule for SetReady is not settled.
B -> CB : SetReadyRequest(session_id, ready true)
CB -> S : SetReady(clientID, true)
S -> G : ReadyToStart(roster, ready)
G --> S : true (two players, all ready)
S -> M : NewMatch(game, join order copy, roles)
M -> G : NewState(order, roles)
G --> M : chess.State (start position, first joiner plays white)
S --> A : StateUpdate(IN_PROGRESS, encoded_view = FEN, active_player_id = A, player_order [A, B])
S --> B : StateUpdate(IN_PROGRESS, encoded_view = FEN, active_player_id = A, player_order [A, B])
@enduml
